```
Based on my research, firearms are typically classified based on their caliber, design, and intended use. Handguns, rifles, and shotguns are common types of firearms. Handguns are small, portable firearms that are typically designed to be fired with one hand. Rifles are long-barreled firearms designed to be fired from the shoulder, and shotguns are firearms that fire multiple projectiles (shot) from a single barrel.
```

